{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עזי וזמרת יה.</b> Onkelos rendered 'תָּקְפִּי וְתֻשְׁבַּחְתִּי' — עָזִּי like עֻזִּי, and וְזִמְרָת like וְזִמְרָתִי. And I am astonished at the language of Scripture, for you find nothing like its vocalization in all Scripture except in three places where it stands adjacent to וְזִמְרָת, and all other places are vocalized with shuruk: ״ה׳ עֻזִּי וּמָעֻזִּי״ (Jeremiah 16), ״עֻזּוֹ אֵלֶיךָ אֶשְׁמֹרָה״ (Psalms 59). And so every two-letter word whose vocalization is malei when it lengthens with a third letter and the second letter does not have a ḥataf — the first is vocalized with shuruk, e.g. עֹז — עֻזִּי, רֹק — רֻקִּי, חֹק — חֻקִּי, עֹל — עֻלּוֹ: ״וְסָר מֵעֲלֵהֶם עֻלּוֹ״ (Isaiah 14), כֹּל — כֻלּוֹ: ״וְשָׁלִשִׁם עַל כֻּלּוֹ״ (Exodus 14). But these three — עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת here, and that of Isaiah, and that of Psalms — are vocalized with ḥataf qamatz, and furthermore in not one of them is it written וְזִמְרָתִי but rather וְזִמְרָת, and all of them are adjacent to ״וַיְהִי לִי לִישׁוּעָה״. Therefore I say, to settle the language of Scripture: עָזִּי is not like עֻזִּי, nor וְזִמְרָת like וְזִמְרָתִי, but rather עָזִּי is a noun, like ״הַיֹּשְׁבִי בַשָּׁמַיִם״ (Psalms 123), ״שֹׁכְנִי בְחַגְוֵי סֶלַע״ (Obadiah 1), ״שֹׁכְנִי סְנֶה״ (Deuteronomy 33). And this is the praise: עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ — He was to me for salvation. And וְזִמְרָת is joined to the Name-word, like ״לְעֶזְרַת ה׳״ (Judges 5), ״בְּעֶבְרַת ה׳״ (Isaiah 9), ״עַל דִּבְרַת בְּנֵי הָאָדָם״ (Ecclesiastes 3). And the term וְזִמְרָת is like ״לֹא תִזְמֹר״ (Leviticus 25), ״זְמִיר עָרִיצִים״ (Isaiah 25) — a term of pruning and cutting: His might and His vengeance of our Elohim was to us for salvation. And do not wonder at the language וַיְהִי — that it was not said הָיָה — for we have verses that speak in this manner; this is its pattern: ״אֶת קִירוֹת הַבַּיִת סָבִיב לַהֵיכָל וְלַדְּבִיר וַיַּעַשׂ צְלָעוֹת סָבִיב״ (I Kings 6) — it should have said עָשָׂה צְלָעוֹת. And similarly in Chronicles: ״וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּעָרֵי יְהוּדָה וַיִּמְלֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם רְחַבְעָם״ (II Chronicles 10) — it should have said מָלַךְ. ״מִבִּלְתִּי יְכֹלֶת ה׳ וגו׳ וַיִּשְׁחָטֵם״ (Numbers 14) — it should have said שְׁחָטָם. ״וְהָאֲנָשִׁים אֲשֶׁר שָׁלַח מֹשֶׁה וגו׳ וַיָּמֻתוּ״ (ibid.) — it should have said מֵתוּ. ״וַאֲשֶׁר לֹא שָׂם לִבּוֹ אֶל דְּבַר ה׳ וַיַּעֲזֹב״ (Exodus 9) — it should have said עָזַב." "<b>זה אלי.</b> In His glory He revealed Himself to them, and they would point at Him with a finger — a maidservant at the sea saw what the prophets did not see (Mekhilta)." "<b>ואנוהו.</b> Onkelos rendered it in the sense of dwelling — נָוֶה: ״נָוֶה שַׁאֲנָן״ (Isaiah 33), ״לִנְוֵה צֹאן״ (ibid. 65). Another interpretation — וְאַנְוֵהוּ in the sense of beauty: I shall tell of His beauty and His praise to all who come into the world, like ״מַה דּוֹדֵךְ מִדּוֹד וגו׳ דּוֹדִי צַח וְאָדוֹם״ (Song of Songs 5), and so the whole matter." "<b>אלהי אבי.</b> This is the same as <b>וארממנהו.</b> <b>אלהי אבי.</b> Not I am the beginning of sanctification, but the sanctification and His divinity upon me is established and standing from the days of my fathers."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:33.433532505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}